// Section: Offer — the incoming-offer popup + its accept/decline/confirm-decline actuation targets.
{
  "$schema": "../../../docs/rules.fragment.schema.json",
  "screens": [
    {
      "id": "doordash.screen.offer_popup_confirm_decline",
      "priority": 19,
      "comment": "#577 quick-decline: bind the confirm dialog's 'Decline offer' button. Its label is on a child text node (textView_prism_button_title, not itself clickable) — clickNodeStrict walks up to the clickable ancestor. #734: anchor the EXACT label 'Decline offer' (was 'decline' substring). The offer popup behind the confirm sheet carries its own bare 'Decline' button under the SAME textView_prism_button_title id; a substring match let both survive the app-owned label check, so the actuation ranker saw a 2-candidate tie and clicked the first-in-tree node (luck, not verification). The exact 'Decline offer' anchor is unique to the confirm sheet's button (every corpus frame renders it verbatim), so the bound target — and thus the ranker's EXACT_TEXT tier — resolves the single correct node; a genuine tie now aborts to manual (#425 fail-closed). The app-owned CONFIRM_DECLINE tap fires (AUTOMATION) only when the dasher enabled quick-declines.",
      "state": {
        "flow": "offer:presented",
        "modeHint": "online"
      },
      "bind": {
        "confirmDeclineButton": {
          // #1114: the 8.97.8 sheet keeps its View chrome (prism_sheet, the "sure you want to
          // decline" copy) but its buttons are now id-less Compose Views — a clickable View whose
          // subtree is `Decline offer` + the countdown; the second arm binds that directly. The
          // Gold variant `Decline & pause store` (fielded 09-18 17:18) is DELIBERATELY excluded
          // from this AUTOMATION target: it also pauses the store for the dasher, a side effect
          // quick-decline consent never covered. A tap on it is still RECORDED as a decline by
          // the `decline_offer` click rule. (A changed definition ⇒ a new capability key.)
          "find": {
            "any": [
              {
                "all": [
                  {
                    "hasIdSuffix": "textView_prism_button_title"
                  },
                  {
                    "hasText": "Decline offer"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "all": [
                  {
                    "isClickable": true
                  },
                  {
                    "hasNoId": true
                  },
                  {
                    "hasAnyText": "Decline offer"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "optional": true
        }
      },
      "require": {
        "exists": {
          "hasTextContaining": "sure you want to decline"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "#595: the require block demands at least one STORE leg (the display_name family the orders parse extracts, excluding 'Customer dropoff'/'Business handoff'). DoorDash's post-accept teardown frame (and arrival pre-render) keeps pay/distance/Accept/Decline chrome but drops the store rows — that frame re-parsed as a NEW degenerate offer (orders=[], itemCount=0, different offerHash) which REPLACED the just-accepted one: ghost accept/timeout, 06-28 seq 141/142 + 06-30 seq 241/242. A frame with no store leg is not an actionable offer; it now classifies UNKNOWN and is never forwarded. Verified against all 43 real offer frames on file (28 device + 15 corpus): every real render carries a store leg.",
      "id": "doordash.screen.offer_popup",
      "priority": 20,
      "state": {
        "flow": "offer:presented",
        "modeHint": "online"
      },
      "branches": [
        {
          "comment": "Branch 0 — the LEGACY View-based card (prism sheet + accept_decline_footer_container; every fielded frame 2026-01 → 2026-09-17). The pre-#1114 rule body moved VERBATIM into a branch so the 8.97.8 Compose card (branch 1) sits beside it under one rule id: same priority, same offer:presented state, byte-identical accept binding definition (so its capability key — and the dasher's consent — is unchanged).",
          "bind": {
            "acceptButton": {
              "find": {
                "hasIdSuffix": "accept_button"
              },
              "optional": true
            },
            "declineButton": {
              "find": {
                "hasIdSuffix": "secondary_action_button_dash_plus"
              },
              "optional": true
            }
          },
          "require": {
            "all": [
              {
                // #1063: the card's two footer buttons — "Decline" and "Accept"/"Add to route" —
                // have anchored this rule since the ruleset's first commit (a18b3b19, inherited
                // verbatim from the pre-#89 Kotlin OfferMatcher): they were the offer popup's most
                // distinguishing chrome, and the pair separated it from every other surface that
                // merely renders the word "Accept". Six real offers in the 09-05 pull fell to
                // UNKNOWN because DoorDash inflates the decline control a beat AFTER the rest of
                // the card: the collar-animation frame carries the full store leg, pay, distance,
                // deadline and a live `accept_button`, but no "Decline" node anywhere in the tree
                // (2026-08-28 15:31:47.105, 2026-09-02 18:32:40 / 18:34:22, 2026-09-03 14:28:32,
                // 2026-09-05 07:45:52 / 07:46:53). Three of those never produced a settled sibling
                // at all — one was ACCEPTED from a card the app had never presented — so the offer
                // was invisible for the whole animation window.
                // Admitting the frame is safe because Decline was never load-bearing on its own:
                // `accept_button` is ALREADY a required conjunct below (via the accept_button /
                // accept_decline_footer_container arm), so "Decline OR accept_button" only relaxes
                // the redundant half of the pair while every other guard stands unchanged — the
                // Accept/"Add to route" text, the footer-id anchor, and the #595 store-leg guard
                // (the two Decline-bearing, store-leg-LESS half-renders in the same pull stay
                // UNKNOWN on that guard, as intended). The post-accept teardown frame cannot leak
                // in either: `offer_accepting` claims it precisely because the Accept affordance is
                // GONE, which this rule still demands. And the early frame is a #830 VARIANT, not a
                // replace — it parses the identical store list, pay, distance and deadline as its
                // settled sibling, so presentationKey AND offerHash match byte-for-byte
                // (`OfferCardPreDeclineTest`); the card enriches in place instead of timing out.
                // Residual, pre-existing and filed as #1069: presentationKey is store-anchored, so
                // two consecutive offers at ONE store are the same presentation identity — the
                // second enriches the first instead of replacing it. Already true between two
                // settled frames; this change only adds one more frame shape that can carry it.
                "exists": {
                  "any": [
                    {
                      "hasText": "Decline"
                    },
                    {
                      "hasIdSuffix": "accept_button"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "exists": {
                  "any": [
                    {
                      "hasText": "Accept"
                    },
                    {
                      "hasText": "Add to route"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "exists": {
                  "any": [
                    {
                      "hasIdSuffix": "accept_button"
                    },
                    {
                      "hasIdSuffix": "accept_decline_footer_container"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "exists": {
                  "all": [
                    {
                      "hasIdSuffix": "display_name"
                    },
                    {
                      "hasTextMatchesRegex": "\\S"
                    },
                    {
                      "not": {
                        "hasText": "Customer dropoff"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "not": {
                        "hasText": "Business handoff"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          "parse": {
            "as": "offer",
            "fields": {
              "payAmount": {
                "coalesce": [
                  {
                    "find": {
                      "all": [
                        {
                          "hasIdSuffix": "text_field"
                        },
                        {
                          "hasTextContaining": "$"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    "read": "text",
                    "transform": "parseCurrency"
                  },
                  {
                    "find": {
                      "hasTextContaining": "$"
                    },
                    "read": "text",
                    "transform": "parseCurrency"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "distance": {
                "find": {
                  "hasTextMatchesRegex": "\\d[\\d.]*\\s*(mi|ft)"
                },
                "read": "text",
                "transform": "parseDistance"
              },
              "deliveryTimeText": {
                "find": {
                  "hasTextStartsWith": "Deliver by"
                },
                "read": "text",
                "transform": {
                  "stripPrefix": "Deliver by "
                }
              },
              "deliveryTime": {
                "find": {
                  "hasTextStartsWith": "Deliver by"
                },
                "read": "text",
                "transform": "parseDeadline"
              },
              "orders": {
                "each": {
                  "all": [
                    {
                      "hasIdSuffix": "display_name"
                    },
                    {
                      "not": {
                        "hasText": "Customer dropoff"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "not": {
                        "hasText": "Business handoff"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "scope": "ancestor(2)",
                "extract": {
                  "storeName": {
                    "find": {
                      "hasIdSuffix": "display_name"
                    },
                    "read": "text"
                  },
                  "orderType": {
                    "conditionalEnum": [
                      {
                        "if": {
                          "exists": {
                            "all": [
                              {
                                "hasIdSuffix": "work_unit_type"
                              },
                              {
                                "hasTextContaining": "Shop for items"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        },
                        "then": "SHOP_FOR_ITEMS"
                      },
                      {
                        "else": "PICKUP"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "itemCount": {
                    "find": {
                      "hasIdSuffix": "display_name_secondary"
                    },
                    "read": "text",
                    "transform": "parseItemCount"
                  },
                  "itemCountUnit": {
                    // #823 Phase 1: denomination of the count above — "UNITS" for a units-only
                    // "(64 units)" render, "ITEMS" otherwise. Read from the SAME node as itemCount so
                    // the pair can never disagree about which token was read; the evaluator uses it to
                    // convert a units count to an items-equivalent for the #556 shop-time estimate only.
                    "find": {
                      "hasIdSuffix": "display_name_secondary"
                    },
                    "read": "text",
                    "transform": "parseItemCountUnit"
                  },
                  "isRedCard": {
                    "presence": {
                      "exists": {
                        "all": [
                          {
                            "hasIdSuffix": "tag"
                          },
                          {
                            "hasTextContaining": "Red Card"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "isLargeOrder": {
                    "presence": {
                      "exists": {
                        "hasTextContaining": "Large Order"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "hasAlcohol": {
                    "presence": {
                      "exists": {
                        "hasTextContaining": "alcohol"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "validate": [
            {
              "assert": "fieldNotNull",
              "field": "payAmount",
              "onFail": "skip"
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "screenshot": {
                "prefix": "Offer - {payAmount}",
                "category": "offer"
              },
              "dedupeKey": "offer-ss-{parsedHash}",
              "throttleMs": 60000
            },
            {
              "log": {
                "type": "OFFER_RECEIVED",
                "payload": "pay={payAmount} dist={distance}"
              },
              "dedupeKey": "offer-log-{parsedHash}",
              "throttleMs": 60000
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "comment": "Branch 1 — #1114: the 8.97.8 COMPOSE offer card, rolled out server-side between 2026-09-17 13:44 (last legacy frame) and 2026-09-18 14:46 (first Compose frame) on the SAME DoorDash build. The tree is id-less: a ComposeView under main_fragment, the card body in a ScrollView (pay `$14.75`, `incl. tips`, one route summary `2 stops (8.5 mi) • 45 min`, per-store rows = a ViewFactoryHolder wrapping the merchant name immediately FOLLOWED by an address sibling `7330 N Loop 1604 W, San Antonio, 78249 TX`, an optional clickable `Shop for 6 items (~7 min)` row after a shop store's address, a `Customer dropoff` holder, the `Guaranteed earnings for completing the offer.` disclaimer, and a clickable footer View whose subtree is `Accept` + the countdown). `Decline` is a clickable View top-right (its subtree is the label alone). Every legacy anchor (accept_button, accept_decline_footer_container, display_name, work_unit_type, display_name_secondary, text_field, `Deliver by`) is absent, so 09-18/19 produced ZERO OFFER_* events across two dashing days while 36 offer frames fell to UNKNOWN or were claimed by side_nav_drawer (the side-nav Compose tree coexists with the card in the same hierarchy — chrome.json5's drawer rule now REJECTS this shape). Anchors are the card's own chrome only (no merchant names — #574 doctrine): ComposeView + exact `Decline` + exact `Accept` + the route-summary SHAPE + a standalone currency figure + the disclaimer prefix + at least one merchant holder followed by an address-shaped sibling. Partial inflation frames (no Accept / no disclaimer / no merchant row — the #1063 class) fail this branch and stay UNKNOWN by design; the two-branch structure keeps the legacy card byte-identical. Known residuals filed on #1114: (a) BADGES (Red Card / alcohol / large order) are resolved at OFFER level — `orderType` and the item count are per store via the holder's sibling(2) shop row; (b) the structural merchant guard is backed by the `collectionNonBlank` validator, so a holder with a blank name skips the branch (→ UNKNOWN) instead of minting a nameless offer; (c) Compose taps produced NO click envelopes in the field (accept is inferred from the pickup-phase exit — `destinationImpliesAccept`; a decline resolves as OFFER_TIMEOUT, the #1104 class); (d) a merchant address that carries no 5-digit ZIP fails the structural guard → UNKNOWN; (e) no `Deliver by` on this card — `timeToCompleteMinutes` carries the platform's route ESTIMATE, never a deadline.",
          "bind": {
            "acceptButton": {
              "find": {
                "all": [
                  {
                    "isClickable": true
                  },
                  {
                    "hasNoId": true
                  },
                  {
                    "hasAnyText": "Accept"
                  },
                  {
                    "not": {
                      "hasAnyText": "Decline"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "optional": true
            },
            "declineButton": {
              "find": {
                "all": [
                  {
                    "isClickable": true
                  },
                  {
                    "hasNoId": true
                  },
                  {
                    "hasAnyText": "Decline"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "optional": true
            },
            "offerBody": {
              // The card body ScrollView (pay, route summary, store rows, the dropoff holder,
              // disclaimer). The Accept footer is a SIBLING of this ScrollView, not a child. The
              // anchor is the disclaimer PREFIX (two fielded variants; 32/32 complete cards) — NOT
              // the dropoff holder, which reads `Customer dropoff` on a single drop but
              // `Multiple dropoffs (2 stops)` on a stack (3 fielded 4-stop offers, Astra round 2).
              // Not a RuleAction target → enumerates no capability. MANDATORY: every economic read
              // below is scoped to it, so a frame with no body never parses (fail-closed) and a
              // background figure/store outside the card can never become this offer's economics.
              "find": {
                "all": [
                  {
                    "hasClassNameEndsWith": "ScrollView"
                  },
                  {
                    "hasAnyTextStartsWith": "Guaranteed earnings for completing the offer."
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          },
          "require": {
            "all": [
              {
                "exists": {
                  "hasClassName": "androidx.compose.ui.platform.ComposeView"
                }
              },
              {
                "exists": {
                  "hasText": "Decline"
                }
              },
              {
                "exists": {
                  "hasText": "Accept"
                }
              },
              {
                "exists": {
                  "hasTextMatchesRegex": "^\\d+ stops? \\(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)? (?:mi|ft)\\) • (?:\\d+ hr(?: \\d+ min)?|\\d+ min)$"
                }
              },
              {
                "exists": {
                  "hasTextMatchesRegex": "^\\$\\d+(?:,\\d{3})*\\.\\d{2}$"
                }
              },
              {
                "exists": {
                  "hasTextStartsWith": "Guaranteed earnings for completing the offer."
                }
              },
              {
                "exists": {
                  "all": [
                    {
                      "hasClassName": "androidx.compose.ui.viewinterop.ViewFactoryHolder"
                    },
                    {
                      "hasFollowingSiblingTextMatchesRegex": "\\b\\d{5}(?:-\\d{4})?\\b"
                    },
                    {
                      "not": {
                        "hasAnyText": "Customer dropoff"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "not": {
                        "hasAnyText": "Business handoff"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          "parse": {
            "as": "offer",
            "fields": {
              "payAmount": {
                "coalesce": [
                  {
                    "from": "offerBody",
                    "find": {
                      "all": [
                        {
                          "hasTextMatchesRegex": "^\\$\\d+(?:,\\d{3})*\\.\\d{2}$"
                        },
                        {
                          "hasFollowingSiblingTextMatchesRegex": "^incl\\. tips$"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    "read": "text",
                    "transform": "parseCurrency"
                  },
                  {
                    "from": "offerBody",
                    "find": {
                      "hasTextMatchesRegex": "^\\$\\d+(?:,\\d{3})*\\.\\d{2}$"
                    },
                    "read": "text",
                    "transform": "parseCurrency"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "distance": {
                "from": "offerBody",
                "find": {
                  "hasTextMatchesRegex": "^\\d+ stops? \\(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)? (?:mi|ft)\\) • "
                },
                "read": "text",
                "transform": "parseDistance"
              },
              "timeToCompleteMinutes": {
                "from": "offerBody",
                "find": {
                  "hasTextMatchesRegex": "^\\d+ stops? \\(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)? (?:mi|ft)\\) • "
                },
                "read": "text",
                "transform": "parseTotalMinutes"
              },
              "orders": {
                "from": "offerBody",
                "each": {
                  "all": [
                    {
                      "hasClassName": "androidx.compose.ui.viewinterop.ViewFactoryHolder"
                    },
                    {
                      "hasFollowingSiblingTextMatchesRegex": "\\b\\d{5}(?:-\\d{4})?\\b"
                    },
                    {
                      "not": {
                        "hasAnyText": "Customer dropoff"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "not": {
                        "hasAnyText": "Business handoff"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "extract": {
                  "storeName": {
                    // A merchant row is admitted by STRUCTURE (a holder followed by an address-
                    // shaped sibling — any text carrying a ZIP, so a non-number-leading street
                    // still admits) and judged by CONTENT: an empty holder or a blank name yields
                    // null here and the `collectionNonBlank` validator skips the whole branch
                    // (→ UNKNOWN) rather than dropping the leg and mis-pricing the stack.
                    "find": {
                      "hasTextMatchesRegex": "\\S"
                    },
                    "read": "text"
                  },
                  "orderType": {
                    // PER STORE: the shop row (`Shop for N items …`) is the clickable View two
                    // siblings after this merchant's holder (holder → address → shop row); a
                    // pickup merchant's sibling(2) is the NEXT holder, whose text never starts
                    // with `Shop for`, so the regex arm yields null and the literal wins. Verified
                    // on the fielded mixed stack (Smoothie King PICKUP + Target SHOP_FOR_ITEMS).
                    "coalesce": [
                      {
                        "find": {
                          "hasClassName": "androidx.compose.ui.viewinterop.ViewFactoryHolder"
                        },
                        "navigate": "sibling(2)",
                        "read": "allText",
                        "transform": [
                          {
                            "regex": {
                              "pattern": "^(Shop for) \\d+ items?\\b",
                              "group": 1
                            }
                          },
                          {
                            "replace": {
                              "pattern": "Shop for",
                              "replacement": "SHOP_FOR_ITEMS"
                            }
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "literal": "PICKUP"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "itemCount": {
                    "find": {
                      "hasClassName": "androidx.compose.ui.viewinterop.ViewFactoryHolder"
                    },
                    "navigate": "sibling(2)",
                    "read": "allText",
                    "transform": {
                      "regex": {
                        "pattern": "^Shop for (\\d+) items?\\b",
                        "group": 1,
                        "then": "toInt"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "itemCountUnit": "ITEMS",
                  "isRedCard": {
                    "from": "offerBody",
                    "presence": {
                      "exists": {
                        "hasText": "Red Card"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "isLargeOrder": {
                    "from": "offerBody",
                    "presence": {
                      "exists": {
                        "hasTextContaining": "Large Order"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "hasAlcohol": {
                    "from": "offerBody",
                    "presence": {
                      "exists": {
                        "hasTextContaining": "alcohol"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "validate": [
            {
              "assert": "fieldNotNull",
              "field": "payAmount",
              "onFail": "skip"
            },
            {
              "assert": "fieldNotNull",
              "field": "distance",
              "onFail": "skip"
            },
            {
              // #595/#1063 at the PARSE level: a structurally present merchant holder with a blank
              // name must not mint an offer (fieldNotNull accepts an empty list / blank names).
              "assert": "collectionNonBlank",
              "field": "orders",
              "subField": "storeName",
              "onFail": "skip"
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "screenshot": {
                "prefix": "Offer - {payAmount}",
                "category": "offer"
              },
              "dedupeKey": "offer-ss-{parsedHash}",
              "throttleMs": 60000
            },
            {
              "log": {
                "type": "OFFER_RECEIVED",
                "payload": "pay={payAmount} dist={distance}"
              },
              "dedupeKey": "offer-log-{parsedHash}",
              "throttleMs": 60000
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "comment": "#888 — the post-accept 'accepting' TEARDOWN frame of the offer card: the dasher pressed Accept, DoorDash swaps the footer for an in-card spinner while it submits, and the card then unwinds. The offer chrome (accept_decline_fragment_container, the Decline button, the pay/distance/store rows) is still rendered but the Accept button is GONE. Every accept produced one of these and it fell straight to UNKNOWN (4 frames in the 07-26 pull: 3 spinner-shaped + 1 footer-gone), so each accept was silently dropping its own follow-frame. RECOGNIZE-ONLY (dev decision 2026-07-27, recognition-gap batch #888): no state.flow, no parse, no bind — the same posture as every other transient overlay rule (dropoff_multi_order_confirm, dropoff_issue_menu, pickup_wait_survey). This is DELIBERATELY not mirroring the sibling offer rules' `flow: offer:presented`: #595 is the standing receipt that re-asserting offer state on a post-accept TEARDOWN frame is how ghost accepts/timeouts get manufactured, and the accept was already latched by the click rule on the frame before. Recognizing it only graduates the capture out of UNKNOWN (see FlowRegionStepper: a flow-less observation advances the observed clock and nothing else). Priority 127 sits AFTER offer_popup (20) and offer_popup_confirm_decline (19), so a live, actionable offer can never be pre-empted by this rule; the rejects below make the two shapes structurally disjoint regardless of order.",
      "id": "doordash.screen.offer_accepting",
      "priority": 127,
      // Any surviving accept affordance means the card is still actionable — that is a
      // LIVE offer (offer_popup's territory), not a teardown. These four rejects are what
      // make the two shapes structurally disjoint, independent of priority order.
      "reject": [
        {
          "exists": {
            "hasIdSuffix": "accept_button"
          }
        },
        {
          "exists": {
            "hasIdSuffix": "accept_decline_footer_container"
          }
        },
        {
          "exists": {
            "hasText": "Accept"
          }
        },
        {
          "exists": {
            "hasText": "Add to route"
          }
        }
      ],
      "branches": [
        {
          "comment": "Shape A — the submit spinner: load_progress's progress_message is inflated over the card while the accept POST is in flight. progress_message alone is NOT sufficient (verified: live offer frames in the same pull carry load_progress/progress_message too, with the Accept button still present) — the rule-level rejects are what separate them.",
          "require": {
            "all": [
              {
                "exists": {
                  "hasIdSuffix": "accept_decline_fragment_container"
                }
              },
              {
                "exists": {
                  "hasIdSuffix": "progress_message"
                }
              },
              {
                "exists": {
                  "hasText": "Decline"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "comment": "Shape B — the footer has already been torn down but the offer body is still rendered (no progress node at all; 2026-07-26 13:27:46 in the pull, and the 06-21 add-on frame in snapshots/sessions/addon_phantom_2026_06_21). Requires a REAL store leg, the same #595 predicate offer_popup uses, so the store-less degenerate frame #595 deliberately routes to UNKNOWN stays there.",
          "require": {
            "all": [
              {
                "exists": {
                  "hasIdSuffix": "accept_decline_fragment_container"
                }
              },
              {
                "exists": {
                  "hasIdSuffix": "secondary_action_button_dash_plus"
                }
              },
              {
                "exists": {
                  "all": [
                    {
                      "hasIdSuffix": "display_name"
                    },
                    {
                      "hasTextMatchesRegex": "\\S"
                    },
                    {
